the president's national security  adviser John Bolton is with us from the  White House he's a former US ambassador  to the United Nations  good morning mr. ambassador good morning  glad to be with you  so u.s. allies say that the president  withdrew from the Iran deal and has no  plan B what is plan B for achieving u.s.  objectives well I think Plan B is  already being implemented when the  President signed the decision memorandum  yesterday he began the process to put  very strict US sanctions back into  effect that'll have a significant ripple  effect on Iran's economy and I think it  demonstrates that we're determined that  we're not going to rely on paper  promises we're going to rely on real  performance to stop Iran from getting  deliverable nuclear weapons and you know  what Orion threat that you didn't  mention this morning that they've made  is to increase spending on their  ballistic missile program which was  never covered by the Iran nuclear deal  now why do they want more ballistic  missiles I can assure you it's not to  launch weather satellites or  communication satellites this is how  they deliver nuclear weapons I think it  shows where the regime really is so the  idea here is that the sanctions will be  so crippling that Iran will cry uncle  give up their enrichment of uranium give  up their meddling in the Middle East and  give up their missile program is that  how this is supposed to work that that's  a piece of it the the broader piece is  the president laid out in his remarks  yesterday  anas were going to be discussing with  our European allies we've already begun  as soon as I finish here I'm gonna get  on a video conference call and continue  the discussions with the British the  French and the Germans about going after  Iran's other malign behavior it's  continuing support for terrorism its  military activities in the Middle East  you know one of the theories of  President Obama and Secretary of State  Kerry was that the nuclear deal by  satisfying Iran by releasing billions of  dollars of economic resources would  change Iran's overall behavior across  the region it's had exactly the opposite  effect right now the u.s. does not have  the support of the European allies on  this does that concern you and if not if  not why doesn't it concern you well  we're going to try and work with the  Europeans we have  absolutely shared common objective which  is to prevent Iran from getting  deliverable nuclear weapons we have a  disagreement over the efficacy of the  Iran deal and that's the reason that  President Trump exited from it just to  give you an example in in short order  the president will be meeting with the  leader of North Korea to discuss  denuclearizing the Korean Peninsula as  North Korea committed to in 1992 which  included not simply giving up nuclear  weapons but giving up uranium enrichment  and plutonium reprocessing this by the  way was the European position when  negotiations with Iran started and it  should have stayed that way are you  concerned ambassador that this could  bring us closer to war with Iran  they're already chanting death to  America over there yeah I don't think it  will bring us closer I think Iran is  bringing us closer to war with its  belligerent activity in Iraq and Syria  you know they've been moving missiles  the Revolutionary Guards Goods force has  been moving missiles into Syria that can  hit any target inside Israel that's why  we've seen recent Israeli strikes it's  that aggressive militaristic behavior by  Iran on the ground in the region that's  the real threat ambassador let me ask  you about North Korea the Secretary of  State there now will he be returning  with those three American prisoners well  I don't want to discuss the specifics I  think secretary Pompeo is on a very  difficult mission we expect he'll be  returning leaving the peninsula in short  order and since he's the negotiator on  the ground out there I think we're going  to wait and leave the initial comment to  him all right ambassador thank you very  much for joining us this morning we  appreciate your time glad to be with you  Thanks
 

